  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Asia Food and Nutrition Security Initiative (SAFNSI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;SAFSNI was conceived at a joint World Bank-DFID  South Asia Heads  meeting in November 2008, and is fully aligned with the principles for  Global Agriculture and Food Security Program (GFASP) agreed at the  L&apos;Aquila Summit in July 2009. The long term goal of SAFNSI is to  improve food and nutritional outcomes across SAR in line with MDG1
 target; this can be achieved only through the adoption of more  effective policies and programs (and relevant behavioral changes at  the community and family level). Towards this end, the development  objective of SAFNSI is to increase commitment of governments and   development partners in the SAR to more effective and integrated  FNS-related policies and investments. The development objective
 will be achieved through three outputs: (i) improved analysis and  evidence the the most effective ways to achieve FNS outcomes; (ii)
 improved awareness of FNS-related challenges, and advocacy for action,  among relevant stakeholders; and (iii) strengthened regional and
 in-country policy and programming capacity to achieve FNS outcomes.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
